{"version": 2, "width": 132, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1787669315, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/zsh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.18755, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m  One district's course catalogue, as a graph\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Prince William County Schools — catalog.pwcs.edu, published openly. No login, no student data.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  7 questions. Every figure is read from the engine as you watch.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.191822, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q0  Where did this come from?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 1 — lookup — a spreadsheet does this perfectly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       Every node carries the catalogue it was published in. Nothing here is typed in by hand.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (n) WHERE n.source IS NOT NULL RETURN n.source, labels(n)[0] AS kind, count(n) AS nodes ORDER BY nodes DESC\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[2.213462, "o", "    \u001b[1msource          \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mkind       \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mnodes\u001b[0m\r\n    ────────────────  ───────────  ─────\r\n    catalog.pwcs.edu  Course       791  \r\n    catalog.pwcs.edu  Requirement  138  \r\n    catalog.pwcs.edu  Subject      127  \r\n"]
[2.213668, "o", "    catalog.pwcs.edu  Pathway      42   \r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m4 row(s) in 22 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[4.715754, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q5  Which courses make up the Information Technology pathway?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 2 — one hop — a join. A spreadsheet is fine\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       One hop — a join. A spreadsheet is still fine here. Note the three named routes through it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (p:Pathway {name: 'Information Technology'})-[e:INCLUDES]->(c:Course) RETURN c.name AS course, e.section AS route, e.credits AS credits ORDER BY e.section, c.name\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[4.719268, "o", "    \u001b[1mcourse                                           \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mroute through the pathway                   \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mcredits\u001b[0m\r\n    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────  ───────\r\n    Advanced Computer Information Systems              Information Support & Services Pathway        1      \r\n    Computer Information Systems                       Information Support & Services Pathway        1      \r\n    Digital Applications                               Information Support & Services Pathway        1      \r\n    Advanced Game Design and Development               Programming and Software Development Pathway  1      \r\n"]
[4.719471, "o", "    Advanced Programming                               Programming and Software Development Pathway  1      \r\n    Game Design and Development                        Programming and Software Development Pathway  1      \r\n    Programming                                        Programming and Software Development Pathway  1      \r\n    Advanced Design, Multimedia, and Web Technologies  Web & Digital Communications Pathway          1      \r\n    \u001b[2m… 3 more\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m11 row(s) in 3 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[7.219591, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q11  Which single course opens the most career pathways?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 3 — the shape of the catalogue — awkward, still possible\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       One course, several different careers. This is the course a counsellor should push hardest, and nothing publishes it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (c:Course)<-[:INCLUDES]-(p:Pathway) RETURN c.name AS course, count(p) AS pathways ORDER BY pathways DESC LIMIT 8\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.219919, "o", "\r\n"]
[7.231782, "o", "    \u001b[1mcourse                                    \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mpathways it appears in\u001b[0m\r\n    ──────────────────────────────────────────  ──────────────────────\r\n    Introduction to Engineering Design (PLTW)   6                     \r\n    Principles of Business and Marketing        5                     \r\n    Production Systems                          5                     \r\n    Introduction to Health and Medical Science  5                     \r\n"]
[7.231853, "o", "    Principles of Engineering (PLTW)            4                     \r\n    Construction Technology                     4                     \r\n    Medical Terminology                         4                     \r\n    Career Strategies                           4                     \r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m8 row(s) in 12 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[9.736469, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q13  What must a student pass to reach Studio Art 5?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 4 — unknown depth — recursive, and you must know the depth to write it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       The depth is not known before you ask. This is where a relational database starts writing recursive CTEs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH path = (:Course {name: 'Studio Art 5'})-[:REQUIRES*1..8]->(need:Course) RETURN length(path) AS steps_back, need.name AS must_pass_first ORDER BY length(path)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[9.739904, "o", "    \u001b[1msteps back\u001b[0m  \u001b[1mmust pass first\u001b[0m\r\n    ──────────  ───────────────\r\n"]
[9.739937, "o", "    1           Studio Art 4   \r\n    2           Studio Art 3   \r\n    3           Studio Art 2   \r\n    4           Studio Art 1   \r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m4 row(s) in 3 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[12.244284, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q15  If a student does not pass Algebra 1, what closes off?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 4 — unknown depth — recursive, and you must know the depth to write it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       The same traversal, inbound. This number is not published anywhere, by anyone. It only exists once the catalogue is a graph.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (blocked:Course)-[:REQUIRES*1..8]->(:Course {name: 'Algebra 1'}) RETURN count(DISTINCT blocked)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[12.255844, "o", "    \u001b[1mcourses closed off\u001b[0m\r\n    ──────────────────\r\n    28                \r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m1 row(s) in 12 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.255904, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.759833, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q16  …and in which subjects?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 4 — unknown depth — recursive, and you must know the depth to write it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m       Chemistry, biology, IB and dual-enrolment science — not just more maths. That is the counselling point.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (blocked:Course)-[:REQUIRES*1..8]->(:Course {name: 'Algebra 1'}) MATCH (blocked)-[:IN_SUBJECT]->(s:Subject) RETURN s.name AS subject, count(DISTINCT blocked) AS closed_off ORDER BY closed_off DESC LIMIT 10\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[14.766599, "o", "    \u001b[1msubject                   \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mclosed off\u001b[0m\r\n    ──────────────────────────  ──────────\r\n    Science - IB Programme      4         \r\n    Math - Electives            3         \r\n    Math - Computer Electives   3         \r\n    Math - Standard             3         \r\n    Science - Dual Enrollment   3         \r\n"]
[14.766893, "o", "    Math - Cambridge Programme  2         \r\n    Math - Advanced Placement   2         \r\n    Science - Standard          1         \r\n    \u001b[2m… 2 more\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m10 row(s) in 7 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[17.270472, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m  Q17  Which course closes off the most, across the whole catalogue?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m       tier 4 — unknown depth — recursive, and you must know the depth to write it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.27056, "o", "\u001b[33m       Every course ranked by what fails to open without it. One traversal over the entire graph — this is the intervention list.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mMATCH (blocked:Course)-[:REQUIRES*1..8]->(k:Course) RETURN k.name AS course, count(DISTINCT blocked) AS closes_off ORDER BY closes_off DESC LIMIT 10\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[17.275814, "o", "    \u001b[1mcourse                                   \u001b[0m  \u001b[1mcourses it closes off\u001b[0m\r\n    ─────────────────────────────────────────  ─────────────────────\r\n    Algebra 1                                  28                   \r\n"]
[17.27585, "o", "    Studio Art 1                               13                   \r\n    Algebra 2                                  11                   \r\n    English 9                                  7                    \r\n    Studio Art 2                               7                    \r\n    Introduction to Engineering Design (PLTW)  6                    \r\n    Biology 1                                  6                    \r\n    Geometry                                   6                    \r\n"]
[17.275865, "o", "    \u001b[2m… 2 more\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[32m10 row(s) in 5 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[19.780252, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m  Everything above came from pages the district already publishes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  The tier-4 and tier-5 answers are published nowhere — not by the district, not by anyone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
